From df2b080201a42f0fc2a54a2ae7ec2c7b384ea492 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:49:12 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: rkisp2: Add the defect pixel cluster correction

The ISP 2.0 passes every hot pixel of the sensor through to the picture
while its DPCC instances stay unprogrammed, which shows as a sky of
single bright pixels on a covered IMX415 at full gain.

Port the RkISP1 defect pixel cluster correction algorithm to the RkISP2
IPA. The tuning sets keep the RkISP1 keys and gain the distance method
of the ISP 2.0 (rk-min-distance, rk-distance-scale), the output
selection bits and a min-gain per set: hot pixels rise out of the noise
floor with the analogue gain, so each set and the fixed set of the
hardware come into use once the gain of the frame reaches their
threshold, and the block is sent again whenever that selection changes.

Seed the imx415 tuning with the method sets of the vendor tuning for
this sensor module, with the sets the vendor enables from ISO 400 tied
to a gain of 8.

Assisted-by: LLM
